sions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. Strength: quick correct decisions, attention. Concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. Concern for others is good for teamwork.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner. Strengths: problem solving, concentration, responsibility. Concerns: moody, loner may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need overall best fit. Likely Candidate B has strong reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, but communication tone issues. Candidate A has leadership but unfriendly. Candidate C has quick decisions and attention but communication issues and egocentric. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving but moody and loner.\n\nWhich is strongest overall? Probably Candidate B: conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good weather assessment (technical), computer skills (technical), but communication tone issue may be mitigated. So I might recommend Candidate B.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: there is none, but we can say \"Given the lack of prior discussion, I propose...\" That's okay.\n\nWe must include explicit facts: \"very conscientious\", \"handles stress very well\", \"good at assessing weather conditions\". Also mention concern: \"sometimes adopts the wrong tone when communicating\". Then argue that strengths outweigh concerns.\n\nThus vote for Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
